**Pricing options of EC2**:
1. On-demand Instance:
--> pay for what you use:
1. Linux or Windows: billing per second after first minute. 72sec: 1 min 12 sec
2. All other OS : billing per hour

--> Has the highest cost but no upfront payment
--> No long term commitment
--> Recommended for short term workload

2. Reserved Instance:
--> upto 72% discount compared to on demand
--> Reservation period: 1 year or 3 years
--> Payment Options: 
       1. No upfront cost
       2. Partial upfront
       3. Full upfront

3. Spot Instance:
 ---> upto 90% discount compared to ondemand
 --> spot instances are unused AWS ec2 capacity


4. Dedicated Instance:
--> A physical server with EC2 instance capacity fully dedicated to your use.
--> most expensive option

5. EC2 Saving plans:
--> commit to a certain type of usage ($10/hour for 1 year or 3 years)

6. Capacity Reservation:
--> Reserve on demand instances capacityin a specific AZ for any duration.




